==Russian==
{{wp|ru:}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE word|ru|nókʷts}}
{{dercat|ru|ine-bsl-pro|ine-pro|inh=2}}
{{inh+|ru|orv|ночь}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*noťь}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-bsl-pro|*náktis}}, ultimately from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*nókʷts}}. {{doublet|ru|нощь|t1=night (archaic)}}, borrowed from Old Church Slavonic.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-ночь.ogg}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Tatiana Kerbush-ночь.wav|a=Saint Petersburg}}
* {{rhymes|ru|ot͡ɕ|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|e||f|loc=ночи́|adj=ночно́й|dim=но́чка,но́ченька}}

# [[night]], [[nighttime]] {{gl|period of time from sundown to sunup}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[ночью|'''но́чью''']]|'''at night'''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[два|2]] [[часа́]] '''но́чи'''|2 a.m. / 2 o'clock '''at night'''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[за́]] '''ночь'''|per '''night''' / for '''a night'''}}

